 R←Test_Misc_012(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;rc;msg;args;space;folder;qdmx
⍝ <UC.GetSpaceAndFolder> works out where a command acts from the "Project:" flag in that command's
⍝ own leading comments:
⍝ * "AddGitIgnore" used to be flagged 0 although its argument IS the project, so the argument was
⍝   ignored and .gitignore went to whichever project happened to be open.
⍝ * "Add" is flagged 0 because its argument is a file, so the project must come from -project=.
⍝ * A command the table does not know about used to make the pick return the whole table, so
⍝   the user was told "LENGTH ERROR" rather than that the build is out of step with the source.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 tempDir←G.U.NormalizeFolder FilesAndDirs.GetTempSubDir'APLGit2-',⊃⎕SI
 (##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/TestData/CiderProject4.zip')ZipArchive.UnzipTo tempDir

 ⍝ The argument of ]AddGitIgnore is the project:
 args←⎕NS''
 args._1←tempDir
 (msg space folder)←G.UC.GetSpaceAndFolder'AddGitIgnore'args
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠≢msg
 →T.GoToTidyUp tempDir≢folder

 ⍝ The argument of ]Add is a file, so -project= decides:
 args←⎕NS''
 args._1←'APLSource/Counter.aplf'
 args.project←tempDir
 (msg space folder)←G.UC.GetSpaceAndFolder'Add'args
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠≢msg
 →T.GoToTidyUp tempDir≢folder
 →T.GoToTidyUp'APLSource/Counter.aplf'≢args._1    ⍝ The file name is left alone

 ⍝ A command <List> does not know about:
 args←⎕NS''
 args._1←tempDir
 :Trap 0
     {}G.UC.GetSpaceAndFolder'NoSuchCommand'args
     →T.GoToTidyUp 1                              ⍝ It must not get here
 :Else
     qdmx←⎕DMX
     →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'drifted apart'⍷qdmx.EM
 :EndTrap

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 (rc msg)←FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce tempDir
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
